---
import MainLayout from "../../../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import ContactSection from "../../../../components/ContactSection.astro";
import LanguageSupportBanner from "../../../../components/LanguageSupportBanner.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../../../data/site";
import { withBase } from "../../../../utils/withBase";
import { getServicePath, getServices } from "../../../../data/services";

const privateServices = await getServices("private", "en");
---

<MainLayout
  title={`IT Help at Home & Home Office in Berlin | ${siteConfig.defaultTitleSuffix}`}
  description="English-speaking IT help at home in Berlin for Windows PCs, Macs, software, Wi-Fi and home networks, new computer setup and data transfer."
  canonicalPath="en/services/private/"
  lang="en"
  alternatePath="leistungen/privatpersonen/"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Home & home office</span>
      <h1 class="section-title">IT help at home and for your home office in Berlin</h1>
      <p class="section-lead">
        When a Windows PC, laptop, Mac, application or home network is getting in the way — or a new
        computer needs to be set up properly — we provide clear, practical help on site in Berlin.
        You do not need to work out the technical cause before contacting us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <LanguageSupportBanner locale="en" />

  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Start with the situation</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Tell us what is not working — or what you want to set up</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Home IT problems often overlap. A slow computer can involve Windows or macOS, an application,
        an account or several things at once. Choose the service that sounds closest to your situation,
        or simply describe the problem if you are not sure where it belongs.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        {privateServices.map((service) => (
          <a class="card service-card-link" href={withBase(getServicePath(service))}>
            <h3>{service.hero.title}</h3>
            <p>{service.seo.description}</p>
            <span class="service-link-label">View service →</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container card-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>When the problem is difficult to classify</h3>
        <p>
          A computer that will not start, has become very slow, keeps crashing, behaves suspiciously
          or blocks access often needs a structured check before the real cause is clear.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Windows PCs, laptops and Macs</li>
          <li>System, software, account and access problems considered together when needed</li>
          <li>Password, account and BitLocker help through legitimate recovery routes only</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3>When several devices and services depend on each other</h3>
        <p>
          Email, printers, backups, Wi-Fi, NAS storage and user accounts rarely operate in isolation.
          We follow the dependencies far enough to solve the actual problem rather than treating each
          symptom as an unrelated task.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Software, email and accounts configured in a practical way</li>
          <li>Wi-Fi, home networks and connected devices considered as one environment</li>
          <li>Backup and data protection included where they are relevant to the work</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3>When replacing the computer is the better next step</h3>
        <p>
          If more troubleshooting or optimisation no longer makes sense, a planned device change can
          be the cleaner solution instead of spending more time on an ageing system.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Needs-based advice for a Windows PC, laptop or Mac</li>
          <li>Setup, normal readable-data transfer, email and peripherals</li>
          <li>A sensible backup step as part of the move to the new device</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="container two-grid">
      <section>
        <span class="eyebrow">How we work</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Understand the problem first, then agree the next step</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          The initial conversation is free. We clarify the problem, affected device and location and
          decide whether an on-site visit, suitable remote help or a closer diagnosis is the sensible
          next step.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>When the request is clear enough, we discuss the expected scope or quotation before the visit.</li>
          <li>If a responsible assessment cannot be made remotely, a paid diagnostic appointment may be needed.</li>
          <li>Additional work, equipment or another visit is agreed before we proceed.</li>
          <li>At handover, we explain what changed and what you need to know in plain language.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          IT experience since 2008. We work across Windows and macOS, software, Wi-Fi/LAN, NAS and
          shared storage, backups, email and accounts, printers and peripherals, and new-device setup
          and migration.
        </p>
      </section>

      <aside class="feature-rail">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">On-site across Berlin</h3>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.4rem; color: var(--ink-700);">
          Include your postcode or district when you contact us. We then agree the appropriate support
          route and appointment with you. Remote help is a supporting option when the task is suitable
          for it.
        </p>
        <div class="district-list">
          {siteConfig.serviceDistricts.map((district) => <span class="district-pill">{district}</span>)}
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="feature-rail">
        <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">Just describe what you need</h2>
        <p>
          You do not need to choose the right service before getting in touch. Tell us what is not
          working or what you want to achieve. Please do not send passwords, PINs, authentication or
          recovery codes, BitLocker recovery keys or remote-access credentials through the enquiry.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are not a hardware-repair workshop and we do not promise data recovery, 24-hour help,
          same-day visits or fixed response times. If a request falls outside our normal scope, we will
          say so clearly rather than overpromise.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactSection locale="en" context="private" />
</MainLayout>
